We are creating a portfolio website with a classical full-size page layout.

Pages:
The top-level portfolio is a single full-width scrolling page. Section labels in the shared bottom navigation pill act as in-page anchors. Case detail pages remain separate full documents. There is no map canvas, camera pan, zoom, connector lines, top header, or right-side menu.

Architecture:
One-page portfolio at `/` with anchored sections, plus separate case-detail documents.
Routes: `/` (Home / Cases / Tools / About / Experience / Contact sections; Experience is on-page only, not in the pill), `/cases/{slug}`.
There are no separate About, Cases list, Contacts, or Blog documents.
Browser Back/Forward work through normal document navigation and URL hashes for in-page sections.

Layout:
- Full-width scrolling page on `--fill-bg-lvl-0` (beige); section content lives in white rounded cards (`--radius-section-card`, 2rem).
- Homepage section order (Figma `12449:8725`): Hero → Cases card → Experience + Tools row → About card → Contact footer.
- One fixed bottom pill (not the Figma inline header position) that blends identity, section anchors, theme, and the primary CTA.
  - Desktop: avatar + name, Home / Cases / Tools / About / Contact, theme switch, Get in Touch.
  - Compact/mobile: collapsed pill with avatar, More, and Get in Touch; expanded state reveals section anchors and the theme switch above the action row.
- Case details keep an in-content Back link to the Cases section on the root page.
- Elements scale proportionally with viewport size (rem + ui-scale tokens). Reserve bottom inset so content is never covered by the pill, including safe-area.

